WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.441
intended to start working right away.

2
00:00:19.321 --> 00:00:22.803
But after she stepped into escape pod Alpha, she quickly got distracted.

3
00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:26.685
"I haven't been in this pod in so long!"

4
00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:31.148
It had a comfortable sleeping unit, along with some fun entertainment options.

5
00:00:31.896 --> 00:00:36.179
But when she looked at the meal-o-matic that dispensed food, she saw it was nearly empty.

6
00:00:36.199 --> 00:00:39.241
"Looks like the food supply is running low.

7
00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.943
I'd better remind Mom to refill it when I'm done."

8
00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:52.250
Ally grabbed one of the last bottles of juba juice from the machine and took a swig.

9
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.971
"Ahh! Still bubbly!"

10
00:00:57.513 --> 00:01:01.576
She turned the repair manual on and got ready to work, but there was something bothering her.

11
00:01:02.508 --> 00:01:04.829
"It's too quiet in here," she murmured.

12
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:09.051
She pressed a button on the dashboard and the pod's computer instantly lit up.

13
00:01:09.071 --> 00:01:12.093
"Alpha," Ally commanded.

14
00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:14.454
"Play some fun music."

15
00:01:15.314 --> 00:01:16.895
An upbeat song filled the pod.

16
00:01:18.356 --> 00:01:21.417
"Satisfactory choice?"

17
00:01:21.897 --> 00:01:22.798
the computer asked.

18
00:01:22.818 --> 00:01:25.539
"Yes! I love this song!"

19
00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:27.540
Ally jumped up to dance around.

20
00:01:43.568 --> 00:01:45.089
When the song ended, she sighed.

21
00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:48.670
"I guess it's time to get to work."

22
00:01:50.551 --> 00:01:53.292
"It's long past time," the computer said.

23
00:01:54.173 --> 00:01:54.973
Ally scowled.

24
00:01:54.993 --> 00:01:57.754
"Are you going to start nagging me too?

25
00:01:58.275 --> 00:02:02.216
Besides, if you're so smart, why can't you fix the comm device yourself?"

26
00:02:02.236 --> 00:02:06.618
"Repair of communication devices is beyond my capabilities."

27
00:02:07.279 --> 00:02:10.040
The computer's lights dimmed as it put itself to sleep.

28
00:02:12.788 --> 00:02:14.770
"That's fine," Ally mumbled.

29
00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:17.532
"I don't need your help or anyone else's.

30
00:02:18.193 --> 00:02:20.935
I'll have this comm device working in no time."

31
00:02:21.455 --> 00:02:24.178
She took another sip of juba juice and sat down to work.

32
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.084
A short while later, Ally had taken the comm device apart, and all the pieces sat in front

33
00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:31.304
of her.

34
00:02:32.665 --> 00:02:34.326
She pushed her tentacles out of her face.

35
00:02:34.346 --> 00:02:36.488
"That wasn't very hard.

36
00:02:37.349 --> 00:02:38.830
And I found the problem.

37
00:02:39.471 --> 00:02:40.451
The fuse was blown.

38
00:02:42.312 --> 00:02:45.174
Now all I have to do is put the device back together."

39
00:02:46.034 --> 00:02:47.015
The computer lit up.

40
00:02:47.035 --> 00:02:51.718
"Be sure to consult the manual before reassembling comm device."

41
00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:59.923
"Thanks, Alpha," Ally replied, "but I took it apart, so I can totally put it back together."

42
00:03:00.823 --> 00:03:01.384
She snorted.

43
00:03:01.404 --> 00:03:04.806
"My parents will be sorry they called me irresponsible."

44
00:03:05.526 --> 00:03:08.188
The computer made a noise that sounded like "Hmm."

45
00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.122
Before long, Ally had finished reassembling the device.

46
00:03:13.142 --> 00:03:16.243
"See, Alpha?"

47
00:03:17.124 --> 00:03:18.765
She proudly flipped her tentacles.

48
00:03:18.785 --> 00:03:21.226
"I told you I didn't need the manual."

49
00:03:22.227 --> 00:03:25.929
"Standing by for test of communication device," the computer said.

50
00:03:25.949 --> 00:03:28.110
"Here we go!"

51
00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.212
Ally turned the device on, expecting it to light up.

52
00:03:32.352 --> 00:03:33.153
But nothing happened.

53
00:03:35.134 --> 00:03:35.894
She tried again.

54
00:03:38.215 --> 00:03:38.936
Still nothing.

55
00:03:40.844 --> 00:03:42.625
"That's funny," Ally murmured.

56
00:03:42.645 --> 00:03:44.146
"I don't know what's wrong."

57
00:03:45.286 --> 00:03:46.307
"Scanning area."

58
00:03:47.027 --> 00:03:48.688
The computer clicked and clacked.

59
00:03:48.708 --> 00:03:52.971
"Detecting nanochip receiver on the floor.

60
00:03:53.791 --> 00:03:57.313
Repeat, detecting nanochip—" "I heard you the first time!"

61
00:03:59.094 --> 00:04:00.595
Ally checked the floor by her feet.

62
00:04:01.475 --> 00:04:04.557
The computer was right—a part from the device was lying there.

63
00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:10.000
"Oops." She didn't want to admit it out loud, but it was time to consult the manual.

64
00:04:10.568 --> 00:04:15.329
As Ally reached across the dashboard to grab the tablet, her arm knocked into the juba juice.

65
00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:19.670
The bottle tipped, spilling sticky juice all over the manual and the dashboard.

66
00:04:20.611 --> 00:04:23.732
The tablet sparked, while the dashboard fizzled and popped.

67
00:04:24.112 --> 00:04:24.712
"Oh no!"

68
00:04:25.152 --> 00:04:25.732
Ally cried.

69
00:04:25.752 --> 00:04:27.193
"What have I done?"

70
00:04:27.213 --> 00:04:32.194
"Sensors indicate you spilled juba juice, and the—" "I know what I did!"

71
00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:33.134
Ally snapped.

72
00:04:33.154 --> 00:04:35.635
"I need to know how to undo it!"

73
00:04:36.255 --> 00:04:39.276
The computer clicked, but Ally cut it off before it could speak.

74
00:04:39.296 --> 00:04:40.816
"No! Don't tell me!

75
00:04:41.177 --> 00:04:42.637
I'll figure it out myself.

76
00:04:43.078 --> 00:04:45.099
But first I'd better clean up this mess."

77
00:04:45.659 --> 00:04:46.900
She hurried to get a towel.

78
00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.882
But somehow the toe of one of her boots got stuck on a rung of the chair.

79
00:04:51.342 --> 00:04:54.945
Ally lost her balance, and her hand slammed into the control lever.

80
00:04:55.405 --> 00:04:58.767
She gasped as she heard the escape pod's engine sparked to life.

81
00:04:59.487 --> 00:05:05.370
Then—whoosh! The pod started to zoom away from the mother ship.

82
00:05:06.271 --> 00:05:07.712
"Alpha!" Ally shouted.

83
00:05:09.588 --> 00:05:10.208
"Stop this thing!

84
00:05:10.469 --> 00:05:12.430
Get me back to my parents' ship—fast!"

85
00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.291
"Unable to comply.

86
00:05:14.751 --> 00:05:17.833
Escape pod is unable to redock with the mother ship at this time."

87
00:05:17.853 --> 00:05:21.575
"What?" Ally blinked, trying to understand what she was hearing.

88
00:05:21.595 --> 00:05:25.137
"Then call my parents so I can ask them what to do!"

89
00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:27.078
"Command does not compute.

90
00:05:27.439 --> 00:05:29.620
Communication device is offline."

91
00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.581
"Oh no!"

92
00:05:32.141 --> 00:05:35.884
Ally cried, watching in horror as the pod hurtled into deep space.
